Never call a child in from play at nightfall|Something else comes in|A mother calls her son in at nightfall; a child comes in, but it isn't her son.|MOTHER; SON; THE CHILD|A doorstep at dusk|It was getting dark|The child is something else|The door, the child, the mother's hand|mimicry|eerie
Don't leave the door open at dusk|Dusk enters|A man leaves the door open at dusk; dusk enters the house and stays, and the rooms get darker.|MAN; WIFE; THE DUSK|A house at dusk|He was bringing in the washing|The dusk is living in the house|The door, the dark rooms, the man's hand|threshold|eerie
Never take a photo at nightfall|The photo is darker than the night|A woman takes a photo at nightfall; the photo is completely black, but she can hear people in it.|WOMAN; HUSBAND; THE PHOTO|A street at dusk|She wanted the sky|The photo is recording the dark|The photo, the voices, the woman's hand|witness|eerie
